    {
      "title": "TVS' Lakshmi Venu seeks partition of family assets, escalating family feud",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tvs-lakshmi-venu-seeks-partition-of-family-assets-escalating-family-feud-126111601217_1.html",
      "description": "Lakshmi Venu, a member of the TVS industrial family, has formally sought a partition of the joint family assets of her father Venu Srinivasan's branch, escalating a succession dispute that could have implications for ownership and control of key businesses within one of India's best-known automobile groups.\nIn a partition notice to her father, Lakshmi called on him, as head of the family, to discharge his fiduciary duties and ensure a \"fair and lawful partition,\" according to a statement from her office on Monday.\nHer mother, Mallika Srinivasan, has publicly backed her claim, exposing a deepening rift within the family over the distribution of its wealth.\nLakshmi maintains that she is entitled to an equal share under the Hindu Succession Act, 1956, as amended in 2005, and has an independent right to seek partition. She has invoked Section 6 of the Act, which recognises daughters as coparceners with the same rights as sons in qualifying Hindu joint family property.\nThe claim covers",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-16T10:32:08"
    }
